resolution = "Use the proposal's explicit retirement option: replace the obsolete standalone wasm/Makefile with a help-only entrypoint. Reject every explicit goal other than help at Make parse time, before any recipe runs, including mixed help/build goals. Default help points developers to repository-root make paxd-build, make paxd-native-libs, and CGO_ENABLED=1 go test -mod=readonly ./wasm/x/wasm/... after native setup. Remove standalone manifest, upstream SDK linker, wasmd daemon, tool install, simulation and generation recipes from this retired entrypoint; production Go tests and other files remain unchanged."
source_proof = "Parse the actual Makefile's assignments, rules, retirement conditional and shell printf argv; assert no stale standalone build or generation commands survive. Parse the documented root commands and follow the real root paxd-build prerequisites and chain.mk build recipe to daemon/paxd, the root Go manifest, root native-library target, module package/tests and node's real WASM keeper/module registrations. No subprocess or external toolchain is needed."
review_only = "Native GNU Make parsing/execution, Go/C/Rust compilation, native linking, module test execution and paxd runtime behavior are review-only for this Python source gate. Assertions prove source connections and command guidance, not a successful native build or deployment. This config-drift finding changes no runtime interface or persistent state and requires no restart-recovery or interface-mismatch scenario. No shell script, unit file or manifest is repaired."
baseline = "Initial git status/diff showed only pre-existing runner .cgignore and spec task-status changes, preserved unchanged. Neither scoped repair file existed; gate.json reported zero builds, zero verifies, zero prior repairs and two available repair cycles; gates.jsonl was absent. No pre-change verify was run and no baseline test failure is claimed: the explicit implementation-first order and exclusive hf-done verification override the older step requesting an unchanged-tree verify. The audit's missing standalone manifest/daemon and upstream linker facts were confirmed by read-only inspection."
